        "original_id": "0da3b81c-96a1-5227-aad3-58b259c8b385",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Stag Inn, Hastings; Faversham, Kent\n- Companies: Shepherd Neame Brewery\n- Organizations: English Heritage\n- Topics: pubs; tied houses; brewery ownership; heritage listing\n\nFacts:\n- Shepherd Neame Brewery is an English independent regional brewery founded in 1698 in Faversham, Kent.\n- Shepherd Neame Brewery has been family-owned since 1864.\n- The Stag Inn in Hastings claims to be the town's oldest surviving pub.\n- The Stag Inn in Hastings is operated as a tied house by Shepherd Neame Brewery.\n- English Heritage has listed the Stag Inn at Grade II for its architectural and historical importance.",
